# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_schema_multidefiner.py" "SCHEMA MULTI-DEFINER GATE: PASS" "schema multi-definer suppression (precision + recall-safe, CREATE-aware)" "schema multi-definer suppression: a DB table CREATED by >1 file in the SAME role -- two migrations both CREATE TABLE orders, or two ORM models both mapping orders -- is AMBIGUOUS; a single querier must NOT false-couple to ALL definers, nor the redundant creators to each other. _cg_schema._schema_graph now counts distinct CREATORS per table SPLIT BY ROLE (sql-creators = migration/DDL sources that CREATE the table: raw CREATE TABLE + Schema::create/create_table/op.create_table/CreateModel/migrationBuilder.CreateTable; model-creators = non-migration ORM models that OWN the table: __tablename__/@Entity/gorm struct/Prisma model/...) and drops every alters/queries/alters_col/queries_col edge to a table with >1 same-role creator, mirroring the sibling P0 guards (openapi #329 / iac #330 / api-contract #332 / config #339 / routes #340, each 66-91% of their false couples were this class). CRITICAL recall guard: only CREATORS count -- a migration that merely ALTERs an existing table (add_column / Schema::table / op.add_column / CREATE INDEX / raw ALTER TABLE) is NOT a creator, so the NORMAL one-CREATE-many-ALTER migration lifecycle (every evolved table in a real Laravel/Rails/Django/Alembic repo) keeps a table SINGLE-creator and FULLY coupled. RECALL-SAFE: single-creator tables are untouched; the crown-jewel moat pair (ONE create migration + ONE model that maps = 1 sql-creator + 1 model-creator) is NOT ambiguous and survives; test/fixture-dir files are excluded as DEFINERS (a real table shadowed by a test factory stays single-creator and KEEPS coupling) but KEPT as raw-SQL QUERIERS (a test that INSERTs into a real table stays coupled). The ambiguous table NODE is still minted (honest); only its coupling edges are dropped. Proven on crafted repos: two-create-migration suppressed, two-model suppressed (an alters-only guard would miss this), single .sql kept, single model kept, 1-CREATE+1-ALTER-migration lifecycle kept, crown-jewel moat kept, test-shadow real coupling kept, test-querier coupling kept, node honesty kept; content-free table names + file paths only" "schema coupling no longer false-couples a querier to every migration/model that happens to CREATE the same table name -- the multi-creator ambiguity is suppressed exactly like the openapi/iac/api-contract/config/routes sibling detectors, while the normal one-create-many-alter migration lifecycle, single-creator recall, the crown-jewel moat, and test-shadow/test-querier recall are all preserved" 16
